cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Complete Lyapunov Functions and Chain-Recurrent Partitions for a Cancer-State Ordinary Differential Equation"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  Can a complete Lyapunov construction (mesh-free / radial-basis ideas in the
  spirit of Argáez, Giesl, and Hafstein) partition a low-dimensional
  cancer-state ODE into chain-recurrent versus transient regions in a way
  that is reproducible from the vector field alone, without interpreting
  basins as treatment response? A planar tumour-effector toy has an unstable
  focus and a periodic orbit of period 19.88. Wendland collocation at the
  selected cut marks 339 of 1156 nodes. The orbit is covered on three grids.
  Along the orbit the rebuilt function changes by 0.024 from peak to peak,
  while a transient drops by 1.31. The focus is resolved only on the finer
  grids. The failing set is not a certified chain-recurrent set. Not a
  medical device.
keywords:
  - complete Lyapunov function
  - chain recurrence
  - meshless collocation
  - Wendland function
  - tumour-effector equation
  - periodic orbit
  - Conley decomposition
  - computational dynamics
  - research-only
